{
  "mn123:0.1": "Middle Discourses 123 ",
  "mn123:0.2": "Incredible and Amazing ",
  "mn123:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn123:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn123:2.1": "Then after the meal, on return from almsround, several mendicants sat together in the assembly hall and this discussion came up among them: ",
  "mn123:2.2": "“It’s incredible, reverends, it’s amazing! The Realized One has such psychic power and might! ",
  "mn123:2.3": "For he is able to know the Buddhas of the past who have become completely quenched, cut off proliferation, cut off the course, finished off the cycle, and passed beyond all suffering: ",
  "mn123:2.4": "‘Such is the birth, names, clans, conduct, teachings, wisdom, meditation, and freedom of those Blessed Ones.’ ",
  "mn123:2.5": "When they said this, Venerable Ānanda said, ",
  "mn123:2.6": "“The Realized Ones are incredible, reverends, and they have incredible qualities. ",
  "mn123:2.7": "They’re amazing, and they have amazing qualities.” ",
  "mn123:2.8": "But this conversation among those mendicants was left unfinished. ",
  "mn123:2.9": "Then in the late afternoon, the Buddha came out of retreat, went to the assembly hall, sat down on the seat spread out, ",
  "mn123:2.10": "and addressed the mendicants: ",
  "mn123:2.11": "“Mendicants, what were you sitting talking about just now? What conversation was left unfinished?” ",
  "mn123:2.12": "So the mendicants told 